hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan  today I mention a question from one of  my forum leaders named Justin who wrote  in asking please share your suggestions  regarding motivation and how do you  personally keep yourself and your  employees motivated so thanks for the  question Justin a really big problem  that a lot of entrepreneurs face I think  every entrepreneur goes through periods  where they think about giving up I think  it's you know not a good idea to keep  going and and you got to go through  those dark days it's one of those dirty  secrets of entrepreneurs that we don't  really talk about a lot you know we're  always saying all the good things about  our business and all the momentum that  we've built but we don't really talk  about how depressing it can be and how  we think about quitting and giving up  and I think again I think every  entrepreneur goes through that at least  at least once and often multiple  multiple times thinking about just going  to get a job and just leaving what  you're doing behind this is too much  work and frustration in terms of what  keeps me motivated what really helped at  the beginning was how I first started  helping entrepreneurs was I was doing  worksheets or workshops sorry so I would  go and do presentations entrence would  come and listen to me and I thought it  was a lot of work and but I really  enjoyed it and I kind of psych myself  out sometimes where before going to  think ah you really want to do this you  know it takes a lot of time but then it  always got a big high afterwards and so  I try to remind myself of all the  positive things that came out of it and  I think the two things that can help you  when you're looking at staying motivated  the first is make sure you think about  the future life that you're trying to  create for yourself so why did you start  your business right there's a reason why  you started it up it's probably to make  a little bit of money but also hopefully  to help people and improve their lives  right if it's just to make money you're  probably not gonna be successful you  want to do something that is gonna  enrich the lives of other people as well  and so whenever I feel down I try to  remind myself of that future life that  that I'm trying to create there's  especially when I was first getting  started and if sometimes find it hard to  get out of bed and get going and do your  work you know when you have a boss your  have to get into work and you have to go  in and you know do your job or you might  get fired but when you're up when you're  your own boss it can be a lot harder to  get that motivation so trying to you  know just remember every morning that  I'm trying to build this life for myself  and I'm trying to help other people and  that kind of gave me a little bit of  extra motivation also trying to get  frustrated with the current situation so  if you're angry that you can't pay your  bills or you can't afford you know  whatever product or service you're  trying to go out and buy that can get  you frustrated give you the motivation  to get going and actually you know take  action the other thing that I found  really helpful for me and this is what  keeps me going now is feedback from  customers so again hopefully you're  building a business that is helping  people and providing a really you know  value add product or service that  improves the lives of other people and  if you're doing that you should be  getting positive feedback from the  customers and for me this is what keeps  me going every day I wake up you know if  I open up my computer I see some notes  from email or social media and people  writing in saying how much they love the  videos or my newsletter or my worksheets  and how it's impacted their lives and  it's you know change their perspective  and giving them new motivation that  keeps me going and you know when you  guys leave comments on the YouTube  videos I want to make more YouTube  videos and same thing with the  worksheets and the newsletter and so I  get that on a daily basis coming in from  all of you guys so thank you like that  keeps me wanting to wake up and do more  for you and so you may not have  immediate feedback yet if you're just  getting started but try to think of some  of the people you've helped maybe you  make a PowerPoint presentation that you  watch in the morning or you just print  off some of the quotes and have the  clothes to your desk about some of the  people you've helped and how you've  impacted their lives and at least for me  I found that really motivating to want  to go and do more you know one of the  greatest joys I think that you can get  in life is helping other people and when  you do it you get a natural Racha high  that you want to go and do again and so  the more you can remind yourself of that  by having some visual cues you know  quotes or pictures from people who you  have helped the more you know easy it is  to go out and want to do it again and  stay motivated but it is tough and so  don't get discouraged if sometimes you  feel down about  business and your life you know it it  happens it's very common but try to make  sure you do something every day to grow  your business and move it forward in  terms of motivating employees what I  found really helpful is two things one  trying to tie them into the bigger  picture of what they're doing so we have  a mission at Evan Carmichael calm we  want to help you know billion  entrepreneurs and there's multiple  people on my team and they all have a  role in helping me do that but they  don't always see how their role ties  into the bigger picture and I think a  lot of entrepreneurs face that challenge  with their team is the staff members  they do their job that could be great  team members but the more you can show  them how their specific task ties into  the bigger picture of helping people the  easier it is for them to stay motivated  often it's easy for the people who are  on the front lines so people who are  dealing with their customers and they're  seen that the positive feedback that's  coming back for them that's that's  easier because they're getting a lot of  positive momentum there but for the guys  in the back end you know like your  programmers or the guys creating the  product your engineers who don't see the  final result and they don't see your  reaction the customers it's helpful to  help tie them into how what they're  doing is helping people and so the more  you can do that the the easier it is to  get them motivated to keep going and  grow themselves the other thing that I  find really helpful leaps from my team  is I get most of the positive stuff in  the business and my team deals with most  of the the crap in the business I think  as entrepreneurs we we you know try to  do the things that we'd like doing and  give off the stuff that we don't and  what I mean by that is all the support  issues all the emails that come in  people asking questions or people having  problems that it doesn't usually come to  me it goes to my team and they'll help  them solve and they do a great job of  doing that when the email so you come to  me are the ones from you guys you're  watching the videos seeing how you know  how great it's been how it's impacted  your life so I usually got all the  positive emails and so what I try to do  is share those with the team so they're  not just getting all the bad emails or  that the support emails are the question  emails but also the emails from you guys  saying how much we've had an impact on  your lives and your businesses and I  find doing that on a regular basis so I  do it monthly  like stats on what we're doing and I'll  send everybody on my team an overall  email of how we did for the past month  how we're doing to accomplish our major  goals and then also some of the we call  them Wow emails but emails that have  come in from you guys who have said how  much we've had a positive impact and  that gives them a better sense of how  they tie into the bigger picture as well  as how we're helping people and the  positive things that we're doing so  makes me feel good about themselves and  want to keep going so hopefully I'll  help the good question I know it's a big  challenge for entrepreneurs but you know  don't get discouraged do something every  day to make your business go forward and  eventually all those little steps will  turn into big steps that you look back  and you'll be amazed of what you can do  so thank you for the question for those  of you watching if you like the video  you know what keeps you motivated if  when you leave comments and thumbs up so  I really appreciate those and if you  have a question about your own business  or about this video feel free to leave  in the comments below I always read  those and your questions are what become  these new videos so feel free to leave  one below thank you and I'll see you in  the next episode  you
 

